WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:11.130
X three is the Circumcenter of triangle A B C: the intersection of the perpendicular bisectors of the three sidelines, equidistant from vertices A, B, and C by the circumradius R.

2
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:21.221
Its trilinear coordinates are cosine A, to cosine B, to cosine C, and its barycentric coordinates are sine two A, to sine two B, to sine two C.

3
00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:33.800
On the central lines layer, X three anchors the Euler line with X two, X four, and X five, the Brocard axis with X six, X fifteen, and X sixteen, and the O I line with X one and X forty.

4
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:41.770
X three is the isogonal conjugate and complement of the Orthocenter X four, and the anticomplement of the Nine-Point Center X five.

5
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:53.700
Notice across the four reference triangles how X three lies inside an acute triangle, lands on the hypotenuse midpoint of the three-four-five right triangle, and moves outside the obtuse Kimberling triangle.
